<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="3ff947df">&lt;p&gt;
    Once an issue has been identified, the project manager is responsible for the issue management process and works
    closely with the project sponsor to agree on the resolution of issues. Please follow the steps below to create the
    Issue Management Plan.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Effective issue management is a critical success factor for the management of a project. Issues are identified at each
    stage of the project and must be resolved in order to for successful project completion. Effective issue management
    allows for:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    • A visible decision-making process;&lt;br /&gt;
    • A means for reaching consensus on questions concerning the project; and&lt;br /&gt;
    • A project audit trail
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Issue Life Cylce&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../../core.mgmt.common.base/guidances/guidelines/./resources/issue_mgmt_flow.png&quot; width=&quot;810&quot; height=&quot;245&quot; /&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Issue Management Process&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    When an issue is identified, it is screened by the project manager or project sponsor, or both. Either of them can
    choose to merge the issue with another existing issue or accept it and log it in a tracker. Once logged, accepted
    issues can either be resolved immediately via an action plan or assigned to a project team member for further
    investigation to determine their impact on the project or be further evaluated.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
    In the evaluation process, each issue may need to further clarified or a recommendation will be made to address it.
    Upon approval by the project sponsor or the appropriate individuals defined in your standard procedures, the
    recommendations resulting from the evaluation are implemented by the project team and the issue is resolved.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;Issue Severity&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The following criteria should be used as a guideline in determining an appropriate severity level to an issue entered
    into the Issue Log:
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;table title=&quot;&quot; style=&quot;HEIGHT: 331px; WIDTH: 610px&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;2&quot; width=&quot;610&quot; border=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Severity Level
            &lt;/th&gt;
            &lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot; abbr=&quot;&quot;&gt;
                Criteria
            &lt;/th&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;p style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
                    High
                &lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                &lt;p&gt;
                    The issue requires immediate attention because it has a significant impact on the project.&lt;br /&gt;
                    Following are some examples:
                &lt;/p&gt;
                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        It will cause a delay to the critical path of the project
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Change the overall direction of the project
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Hinder the quality of the deliverable
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Increase the cost of the project
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;
                        Impair the solution
                    &lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Medium
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                The issue requires attention; however, it may not be immediate. It presents a potential significant impact
                on the project unless resolved in a timely manner. If the issue is not resolved within X weeks, it
                automatically becomes a ‘High’ severity issue.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
        &lt;tr&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                Low
            &lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;
                The issue does not require immediate attention. It needs further investigation or clarification. If the
                issue is not resolved within 2 weeks, it automatically becomes a ‘Medium’ severity issue. If the issue is
                not resolved within a month, it automatically becomes a ‘High’ severity issue.
            &lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
    &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
